{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PLAN SCOPE CORRECTED before review, measured against merged origin/main (fdc2695a1) rather than assumed.\n\nJ6's change 1049 landed more than this plan anticipated. adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py already exists\n(273 LOC, with JiraDataCenterBackend, the @register(\"jira-datacenter\") factory, and _search_users_by_username),\nand adapters/__init__.py already imports it at line 16, so select_backend(\"jira-datacenter\") resolves and J6\npins that with its own registry test. The old Scope listing backend.py and the registration as NEW work would\nhave sent the reviewer looking for work that is already done.\n\nWhat is genuinely still missing — both read off the merged tree, not inferred:\n 1. _config_schema.py's reconciler.backend validator is STILL `_as_choice(v, k, {\"jira\"})`. So the DC backend\n    is REGISTERED BUT UNREACHABLE: the registry resolves it, config rejects it. That gap is this story's core.\n 2. test_backend_contract.py's fixture is STILL params=[\"fake\", \"jira\"] — the DC backend has never been run\n    against a single generic port assertion.\n 3. The J2 import checker rejects adapters/jira/ importing adapters/jira_datacenter/, but there is NO rule for\n    the other direction — a DC module importing adapters/jira/ passes today. That reciprocal half is this\n    story's AC, and it is genuinely absent.\n 4. _optionality.yml's clean-core-wheel absent-module list still lacks \"jira\" (confirmed at line 108).\n\nThree stale pointers also fixed rather than left to mislead: the `_config_schema.py:697` line reference (the\nvalidator now sits near :604 — the plan now says to find it by symbol, not line), and the\n`tests/live_jira_dc/test_reconcile_pass.py` path (must be `tests/external/live_jira_dc/` — the same wrong-path\nerror J6's plan had to correct; outside tests/external/ it would be collected by per-commit CI on runners with\nno Docker or Jira and break the build for everyone).\n\nAdded to the plan from J6's execution experience: a live module must FAIL LOUDLY, not skip, when the harness is\nreachable but the [jira-datacenter] extra is absent. J6 proved that matters — the all-skip canary counts\ncollected-vs-executed GLOBALLY per session, so a sibling module's executing tests mask an all-skip and the job\nreports green having validated nothing.\n\nNO acceptance criterion was changed, added, or removed. The corrections are to Context/Approach/Scope only."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785438086227297001,"uuid":"b2f84544-7c3f-4195-95ed-98ebd97ecff0"}